-- Q1242: Nontaxable Dispositions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1033(a)(2), gain on an involuntary conversion is recognized only to the extent that conversion proceeds exceed the cost of qualified replacement property. Here, realized gain is $300,000 ($900,000 - $600,000) and the amount not reinvested is $50,000 ($900,000 - $850,000), so only $50,000 is recognized. Under Section 1033(b), the replacement property''s basis is its cost ($850,000) reduced by deferred gain ($250,000), yielding $550,000.
Wrong (B): $600,000 represents the original adjusted basis. It ignores the basis reduction required by Section 1033(b) to preserve the $250,000 of deferred gain.
Wrong (C): $850,000 is the cost of the replacement property, but the basis must be reduced by the $250,000 of deferred gain under Section 1033(b).
Wrong (D): $900,000 is the condemnation proceeds received, not the basis of the replacement property.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1242;

-- Q1243: Nontaxable Dispositions [hard/L2]
