UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Total gain is $60,000 ($100,000 - $40,000). Under Section 453(i), the $50,000 of Section 1245 depreciation recapture is recognized in full in Year 1 regardless of payment timing. The remaining $10,000 of Section 1231 gain is reported under the installment method. The gross profit ratio for the installment portion is 10% ($10,000 / $100,000 selling price adjusted for recapture). Year 1 installment gain on the $25,000 payment is $3,750, so total Year 1 gain is $50,000 + $3,750 = $53,750.
Wrong (A): $15,000 would result from applying an incorrect 60% gross profit ratio to the $25,000 payment, ignoring the recapture acceleration requirement.
Wrong (B): $25,000 equals only one installment payment and does not account for the accelerated recapture of $50,000 in Year 1.
Wrong (C): $50,000 represents only the Section 1245 recapture and omits the $3,750 installment gain on the Year 1 payment.$EXPL$
