UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Son''s cost basis is $60,000 (the purchase price). Without Section 267(d), Son''s gain would be $60,000 ($120,000 - $60,000). Under Section 267(d), Son may offset his gain by the amount of Mother''s previously disallowed loss ($30,000 = $90,000 - $60,000). The recognized gain is therefore $60,000 - $30,000 = $30,000.
Wrong (B): $60,000 is the gain before applying the Section 267(d) offset. It ignores the benefit Son receives from Mother''s disallowed loss.
