  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Corporations A and B are related parties under Section 267(b)(3) because the same individual owns more than 50% of each. Under Section 267(a)(2), Corporation A cannot deduct the accrued rent until Corporation B (cash basis) includes the amount in income. Corporation B receives payment in Year 2, so the deduction is deferred to Year 2.
