  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): With a 37.5% Section 250 deduction, the taxable portion of GILTI is 62.5% (100% - 37.5%). Applying the 21% corporate rate to that taxable portion yields an effective rate of 13.125% (21% x 62.5%). This is an increase from the prior effective rate of 10.5% when the deduction was 50%.
Wrong (A): 10.5% was the effective GILTI rate when the Section 250 deduction was 50% (21% x 50% = 10.5%). That rate applied for tax years beginning before 2026.
Wrong (C): 15.75% would imply a 25% deduction (21% x 75%), which is not the enacted percentage under any provision of the TCJA.
Wrong (D): 21% would apply only if there were no Section 250 deduction at all. The 37.5% deduction reduces the effective rate below the full corporate rate.$EXPL$
