-- Q3920: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 422(a), when ISO shares are held for at least two years from the grant date and one year from the exercise date, the entire gain upon sale is treated as long-term capital gain. The spread at exercise ($45 - $20 = $25 per share x 500 shares = $12,500) is not recognized as ordinary income if both holding periods are satisfied, though it is an AMT preference item in the year of exercise.
Wrong (A): Ordinary income treatment applies only to a disqualifying disposition (selling before meeting both holding periods). Here the holding requirements are met.
Wrong (C): Short-term capital gain would apply if the shares were held for one year or less after acquisition, but the facts state both holding periods are satisfied.
Wrong (D): A sale of stock is a taxable event. The gain is recognized at the time of sale, not deferred until a subsequent gift.$EXPL$
