-- Q3922: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 83(b), an employee may elect to include the fair market value of restricted stock ($30 x 1,000 = $30,000) in ordinary income at the time of the grant, before the stock vests. The election must be filed within 30 days of the transfer. Any subsequent appreciation above $30 per share is taxed as capital gain when the shares are ultimately sold.
Wrong (B): Without a Section 83(b) election, the employee would wait until vesting. However, the question specifies the election is made, triggering immediate ordinary income recognition.
Wrong (C): The Section 83(b) inclusion is ordinary income, not capital gains income. The election accelerates the ordinary income recognition to the grant date.
